      "id": "claim_c67ab2e63e244031b123a7afae1042e3",
      "statement": "Every in-repo body link in the bundle must be written relative to the file containing it, because a site-root-absolute link resolves against the forge's site root and 404s. Conformance rules V14 and V15 fail the absolute form outright and fail any relative link that does not resolve from its own file's directory; they were added after 204 such dead links survived across 61 of the bundle's 77 files while okf-lint passed, because it only verified the `resource` front matter (item 491).",
