    {
      "id": "claim_ac67c6ca90354dbd911d5bb8fa1aae35",
      "statement": "The two gates that police the bundle — `pnpm nx okf-lint infrastructure-as-code` for conformance (rules V1–V16) and `pnpm nx okf-governance infrastructure-as-code` for policy, protection, classification and Claims scope (rules G0–G13, where G13 keeps Claims sidecars off authoritative pages) — run offline and keyless and are fail-closed: an absent or partially-written bundle, or a missing governance file, is a violation rather than a skip, and there is deliberately no skip flag and no allowlist, so a rejected page is fixed in openwiki/INSTRUCTIONS.md and regenerated rather than accepted in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/wiki-maintenance.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:eefbce98c8da9e2e807861e00b6ec894d2e313f6a5af125ff5de8b21a00a652e"
