    {
      "id": "claim_2383467a07de4fc8a42fbcecf7b73a88",
      "statement": "The derived-versus-authoritative classification is a ratified governance decision, not just a convention: ADR-0003 makes Grounded Claims and the `protected.yaml` fingerprints complements with disjoint scopes — Claims live on derived pages only, fingerprinted passages on authoritative pages only, and no page is both — enforced by governance rule G13 (`claimsScopeFindings`), which is why the quickstart routes a reader to that decision when explaining what a page's `resource` field means.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/ADR-0003-claims-and-fingerprints.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:6fa85e5a873bebbdf7c26056e056dd13f7fe5c2f062e45d5d0a93f7058e78cf3"
