    {
      "id": "claim_573775a4127d4cbab542ae4f1d653113",
      "statement": "`specs/**` is declared *analyzable, not a coverage target*: specs are read freely as context but there is deliberately no concept per feature, because a merged feature's specification is a historical record superseded by the code it produced. `specs/*/HANDOFF.md` is the named exception, carrying live measured knowledge rather than history. A spec is also never the current state — when it disagrees with a runbook, a decision record or the code, the later source wins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/044-openwiki-automation-migration/spec.md#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf82f0ddcde8b3e377797ab3ec8699ade2a112a3f3cdcad67e5125f8f28426d5:"
